WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.240
A marriage document, two names at the top.

2
00:00:03.290 --> 00:00:07.100
The seal comes down, and
the woman's name fades away.

3
00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:12.220
Before 1870, a wife's property
passed to her husband's control.

4
00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:15.660
Full control came only in 1882.

5
00:00:15.710 --> 00:00:20.500
Four novels sit on a
shelf, from 1811, 1847,

6
00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:23.800
1891 and 1925.

7
00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:29.160
So how do novels show women's lives,
when the law gave them so few rights?

8
00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:33.600
In this mission, you'll walk with a woman
through London who feels herself become

9
00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:37.040
"invisible; unseen; unknown".

10
00:00:37.090 --> 00:00:40.150
And you'll hear a young wife
judged on her wedding night,

11
00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:42.600
by the man she has just married.

12
00:00:42.650 --> 00:00:47.990
Your mission: explain how these novels
show women's lives under those laws.
